I am leaving this review because Erin Miller Schumann is currently listed as a clinician with Solidarity Therapy. I want to make clear that the experiences described in this review did NOT occur at Solidarity Therapy. They occurred in 2022, when I was a minor and Erin was working at Life Skills Therapy in Langley.

Erin Miller Schumann is currently listed as an RCC (Registered Clinical Counsellor) and RCAT (Registered Canadian Art Therapist) and works with clients including youth. My experience with her as a young client was extremely concerning, and I believe it is important for prospective clients and parents to be aware of it.

During my time as her client, I experienced repeated boundary violations that I did not understand were inappropriate at the time. Among other things, she:

• allowed me to vape in the counselling room;
• encouraged an unusually open line of personal communication, including allowing me to contact her by phone and text at essentially any time;
• discussed her work as a sex therapist with me while I was a minor;
• shared highly personal information about her own sexual experiences and history with me;
• disclosed personal information about her mental health to me; and
• disclosed deeply personal information about her own suicidal thoughts to me.

Looking back on these interactions as an older person, I recognize that these were not appropriate boundaries for a therapist to have with a minor client. I felt that the relationship became inappropriate and that I was being groomed. At the time, I was 14 and did not have the knowledge or power to understand or appropriately respond to what was happening.

Again, none of these events occurred at Solidarity Therapy, and I am not alleging that Solidarity Therapy was involved in them. I am posting this review because Erin is currently affiliated with Solidarity Therapy and I believe potential clients—particularly young or vulnerable clients—deserve to be able to make an informed decision about who they receive care from.

I am also pursuing this matter through the appropriate professional complaint channels.
